13. The trial court and the appellate Court further held that the contention of defendant No. 1 that his father was never evicted from the suit land by landlord has been belied by Ext. 7, a barga Kabuliyat executed by defendant No.1 himself in favour of the plaintiffs admitting the plaintiffs' title to and possession in the suit land; 

 It is true that admission in a Criminal proceeding cannot be used in a civil suit but the barga Kabuliyat Ext.7 executed by defendant No.1 himself in favour of the plaintiffs in the suit land cuts at the very root of the defendant No. l's case. 

 15. The High Court Division did not at all notice the vital document Ext.7 a barga Kabuliyat executed by defendant No. 1 himself in favour of plaintiffs admitting plaintiffs' title to and interest and possession in the suit land
